   197	## 3. Theorem AV and proof
   198	
   199	**Theorem AV.** Let c be as in Proposition U(ii). There are absolute n₀ and C such that:
   200	
   201	- (i) **Completeness.** For every N ≥ 2, LAD_n (n = bit length of N) outputs the complete
   202	  prime factorisation of N. It is deterministic and sees only N.
   203	- (ii) **Worst case.** On every n-bit input the cost is
   204	  ≤ HH(N) + C n^{c+4}2^{7n/36} + C n^{O(1)}2^{3n/20}. That is
   205	  O(N^{1/5}log^{16/5}N/(log log N)^{3/5}), Harvey–Hittmeir's bound.
   206	- (iii) **Average over S_n.** For n ≥ n₀,
   207	
   208	    (1/|S_n|)·Σ_{(p,q)∈S_n} cost(pq) ≤ C·n^{c+1}·log n·2^{n/6} = N^{1/6}(log N)^{c+1}(log log N)·O(1).
   209	
   210	  With D′'s original n²/H² coverage bound instead of Lemma R, the factor is n^{c+2}log n.
