     1	"""OPERATIONAL: DCL-det, the deterministic divisor-cover Lehman algorithm.
     2	
     3	Receives only N and a public Design (a function of the bit length n; see
     4	params.py).  Never uses p, q, phi(N), group orders or any factoring /
     5	primality routine.  Base beta = 2 (fixed, no randomness).  Every inversion
     6	mod N is gcd-checked, every nontrivial gcd is returned.
     7	
     8	Algorithm (notes/dcltheorem_results.md, section 2), for each block k = 0..K-1:
     9	  1. L = prod_{l in P_k} l^2;  u_l = 2^{L/l^2} for all l by a balanced
    10	     all-but-one exponent tree;  gamma = 2^L.
    11	  2. For each l in P_k and (A, B) in V: a = A N B^{-1} mod l; if a is a
    12	     nonzero square mod l (Euler), r = a^{(l+1)/4} (l == 3 mod 4) and the
    13	     roots are {r, l - r}.  For each root: s = N r^{-1} mod l^2,
    14	     c = (B r + A s) mod l^2, whole-range window [g_lo, g_hi] from the exact
    15	     integer bounds Lo_v <= B p + A N/p <= Hi_v on the balanced range, and
    16	     giants  G_{tau,j} = u_l^{B + A N - c} gamma^{-(g_lo + j m)},
    17	     0 <= j < ceil(W/m).
    18	  3. Babies gamma^i, 0 <= i < m;  f(X) = prod (X - gamma^i);  f(G) for every
    19	     giant by a remainder tree;  d = gcd(f(G), N);  output d if 1 < d < N.
    20	Output None (FAIL) if no block produced a factor.
    21	
    22	Cost counters (Metrics): mulN (multiplications mod N, square-and-multiply
    23	counted exactly), mul_small (mults mod l or l^2), bigmul_bits (sum of operand
    24	bit lengths of integer products in the exponent product tree), poly_cost /
    25	poly_ops (stage 3; see stage3.py), gcdN, invN, isqrt_ops.
    26	"""
