     2	
     3	OPERATIONAL helpers: see only N and ring elements.  Only multiplication and
     4	division by MONIC polynomials are used, so everything is valid over the ring
     5	Z/N with N composite.  No gcd/xgcd/factor of polynomials over Z/N is called.
     6	
     7	Cost charging (notes/dcltheorem_prereg.md, metric E):
     8	  poly_cost += (d + 1) * ceil(log2(d + 2))   for every product / remainder whose
     9	               result (product) or dividend (remainder) has degree d
    10	  (FFT-model M(d) in Z/N-multiplication equivalents).  Scalar multiplications
    11	  mod N are charged in mulN; gcds with N in gcdN.
